  "articleBody": "Tearing down a wall sounds exciting when designing an open-concept living area, but structural mistakes can cause ceiling sag, cracked drywall, or door frame sticking throughout your home.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps:\n- Multiple floors or roof weight directly above: If joists run perpendicular into the wall or line up with structural supports on lower levels, the wall is load-bearing and needs engineered replacement beams.\n- Manufactured trusses or engineered lumber: Altering manufactured framing components requires precise calculations and strict adherence to structural requirements.\n- Relocating mechanical or electrical chases: When an interior wall conceals plumbing vents, wiring, or HVAC ducts, the framing rework must coordinate seamlessly with rough-trade contractors.\n- Local permit requirements: In many municipalities, modifying structural walls requires engineered plans, permit filings, and mandatory framing inspections before drywall installation.\n\nAttempting to remove or resize load-bearing members without proper temporary supports risks your safety and your home's foundation. An experienced contractor handles the structural work properly from day one.\n\nIf you are planning to reconfigure your home's layout, call Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 for a professional framing consultation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}